    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d388">

                <pb facs="0350" n="342" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg342"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/983: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief of the United States Asiatic
                        Fleet</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Yarnell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chief of Naval
                        Operations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Leahy</hi>)<anchor n="47" xml:id="d388-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-20T09:15:00+08:00">September 20, 1937—9:15
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 20—7:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>0020. Am advising Admiral Hasegawa that our naval vessels will remain Nanking as
                    long as any of our nationals are in the city and warning him to advise his
                    aviators accordingly.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
